ive_call_7c356de1dbcb_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_7c356de1dbcb","agent_id":"main","sequence":92,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_dd63aed0149d","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:18.994116+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:42.884534+00:00","duration_ms":23890.41220000945,"text":"**Clarifying snowfall analysis**\n\nI need to determine that 71% and 79% figures to assess how unusual the conditions are. The rankings suggest it's in the upper third for cool seasons, indicating a moderately snowy winter, not extreme. I'll create a comprehensive table with about 7 rows to reach 600 words instead of the user's desired 400. Lastly, I will ensure to source citations, clarify data limitations, and keep everything organized for reproducibility.**Organizing report creation**\n\nI think I need to record the hashes for artifact annotation without relying on report dependency IDs for the output. It makes sense to create a second artifact in markdown format that includes the full methods, provenance, and all sources used. This way, everything remains clear and well-documented for future reference. I'll make sure the report is thorough and accessible, ensuring all necessary information is included for the user.","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":94,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_f1d0471b545e_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_f1d0471b545e","agent_id":"main","sequence":95,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_52c69ec44d5f_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_52c69ec44d5f","agent_id":"main","sequence":97,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_f005fa5de2e6","type":"text","text":"**Alta-Collins received 635.5 inches of new snow in October–April 2023–24—about 17% above the historical mean, but not exceptionally snowy within the NDP record.** Among winters with complete October–April coverage, it ranks **6th of 18**, including 2023–24.\n\nThe chart above shows every available winter, with incomplete historical sums marked in gold.\n\n### How unusual was it?\n\nThe historical collection covers **24 earlier winters, 1999–2000 through 2022–23**. Because some lack October observations, two comparisons are useful:\n\n| Comparable window | 2023–24 snowfall | Earlier-winter mean | Above mean | Rank, including 2023–24 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| **October–April**, using only 17 complete earlier winters | **635.5 in.** | 541.7 in. | **17.3%** | **6th of 18** |\n| **November–April**, complete in all 24 earlier winters | **606.5 in.** | 516.1 in. | **17.5%** | **6th of 25** |\n\nThe gap-free November–April comparison puts 2023–24 above **19 of 24 earlier winters**, roughly the 79th percentile relative to that historical sample. Both comparisons support the same conclusion: **a snowier-than-usual winter, but not an extreme one**. For perspective, 2022–23 totaled **903.0 inches** over October–April. These results come from summing the files’ 12-hour new-snow observations; the seasonal values and coverage counts are retained in the comparison CSV.\n\n### Coverage limits\n\n- **Seven historical winters have missing October observations:** 1999–2000, 2000–01, 2001–02, 2003–04, 2005–06, 2019–20 and 2020–21. Their chart bars are partial sums—not complete totals. I did **not** fill missing observations with zero.\n- **2023–24 is complete:** all **426 expected 12-hour periods** are present. November–April is also complete in every historical winter, making it the strongest comparison using the entire archive.\n- **This is an October–April study-plot record, not a full-year resort total.** It measures accumulated new snowfall at the mid-mountain Alta-Collins plot, not snow depth. May–September snowfall is outside the comparison.\n- **Processing differs slightly:** the historical README describes quality control and conversion of trace snowfall to zero; the 2023–24 README describes raw Ski Patrol observations without additional quality assurance. See the [historical documentation](workspace-file:/D:/CLIO-Develop/ndp-shareable-20261019/alta-snowfall-17/sources/historical_README.txt) and [2023–24 documentation](workspace-file:/D:/CLIO-Develop/ndp-shareable-20261019/alta-snowfall-17/sources/2023-24_README.txt).\n- These collections support an **archive-relative ranking**, not an all-time Alta ranking or a “one-in-X-year” return period.\n\n**Files retained:** `Alta seasonal comparison` (CSV) and `alta_comparison_notes.md`, including the detailed gap audit, methods and source attribution.","agent_id":"main","sequence":99,"stream_source":"live","channel":"answer"},{"id":"part_fadbcb62c7b1","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_0aa3909d91fe4c8b872de87800dc4853","agent_id":"main","sequence":100},{"id":"part_f0072626a3a8","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_fd37003b759648d59aad0cd0b1485a0c","agent_id":"main","sequence":101}],"run_id":"84bdc146-0cc6-404d-9c9d-dee16b588394","usage":{"input":1891614,"output":10866,"cache_read":1721344,"cache_write":0},"stop_reason":"end_turn","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:35.414155+00:00"},{"id":"76bc3ce2-4dce-44cb-93e0-3b57b07a3203","session_id":"sess_4e74d38f7a9d","role":"user","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:09:54.820003+00:00","blocks":[{"id":"part_19ce3696dad6","type":"text","text":"Was that driven by especially snowy months, or was snowfall elevated throughout the winter? Let me explore the monthly comparison.","channel":"answer"}],"run_id":"76bc3ce2-4dce-44cb-93e0-3b57b07a3203","model":{"provider_id":"codex","model_id":"gpt-6.1-sol"},"usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cache_read":0,"cache_write":0}},{"id":"msg_asst_115369c4dfec","session_id":"sess_4e74d38f7a9d","role":"assistant","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:14:55.297736+00:00","blocks":[{"id":"live_injection_c966915e0e87","type":"injection","source":"todos","text":"## Todo checklist (your current task list — reconcile before finishing)\n\n[x] Find Alta-Co