ce_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"state":"completed","change":"removed","uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"todo-3","type":"check","media_type":"","text":"Compute the 2023–24 comparison against comparable historical winters.","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"state":"completed","change":"removed","uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"todo-4","type":"check","media_type":"","text":"Show the comparison with source citations and explicit coverage limits.","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"state":"completed","change":"removed","uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":125.57554244995117,"started_at":"2026-10-19T07:10:30.148851+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:10:30.274426+00:00"},{"id":"call_bb72c327e447","session_id":"sess_4e74d38f7a9d","run_id":"76bc3ce2-4dce-44cb-93e0-3b57b07a3203","name":"load_skill","title":"Load skill","state":"succeeded","input":{"kwargs":{"file":"","files":null,"skill_id":"review-visual-presentation"}},"output":"# Skill: review-visual-presentation\nSkill directory (use as SKILL_ROOT): D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\clio-ndp-source\\src\\clio_agent\\gact\\builtin_skills\\review-visual-presentation\nUse visual interaction to investigate a question and to improve what a person\nwill see. The loop is: inspect the evidence and current view, change a declared\ncontrol or component, inspect the resulting image, reason, and refine.\nChoose changes that resolve a concrete uncertainty or presentation problem.\nThis applies to maps, charts, tables, images, models and interconnected reports.\n\nFor a substantial authored dashboard or diagram, close this concrete loop:\n\n1. Open the actual published viewer, inspect its current capture target, and\n   capture the overview at the width the person will use.\n2. Look at the returned image, not just its URI, source JSON or tool success.\n   Check whether the main idea is apparent, text is readable, the whole diagram\n   fits, and empty space or narrow columns obscure relationships. Ask whether\n   a full-width view, equal panels or a simpler arrangement would explain it better.\n   Include the surrounding frame/component headings, not only the plotted marks:\n   a title cut off with an ellipsis is a defect even when the graph fits. Check\n   whether labels can actually be read at this size, rather than merely seen.\n3. Identify a concrete defect and change the source or a declared view control.\n   Changing column counts is useful only when it fixes the observed problem.\n4. Capture the revised view and inspect its image to confirm the correction.\n   Check an expanded view as well when the docked and expanded arrangements differ.\n5. Exercise important declared controls or linked selections. For a workflow\n   folder link, verify the target with filesystem tools. If interaction tools are\n   available, check that clicking selects that folder in Files. Claim a navigation\n   check only when it was observed; a highlighted box alone does not prove it.\n\nRepeat while a material defect remains. State the actual visual checks and any\nunresolved limitation. Schema validation, a capture receipt and an uninspected\nimage do not establish visual quality. A small inline diagram does not require\nbuilding a dashboard or following an elaborate layout recipe.\nKeep docked and expanded findings separate: readability in an expanded image\ndoes not establish readability in a narrow pane. When text remains too small,\nrevise the view or state that limitation instead of declaring the review clear.\n\nRead the current surface with `inspect_a2ui_surface` and load the relevant\nactive catalog schemas. `update_a2ui_components` replaces complete definitions\nfor the named components; preserve the other properties, references and links.\n`update_a2ui_data_model` changes a declared binding. Reuse shared filter and\nselection semantics rather than inventing another interaction model. For definition\nchanges to saved dashboards, edit the source document and publish a new immutable version.\n\nDistinguish server state from a rendered view. A producer's `rendered=true`\nmeans the definition was accepted, not that you inspected its pixels.\n`inspect_a2ui_surface` reports fresh mounted viewers, declared bindings,\ncurrent values, cameras, active tabs, data references and readiness. Choose\nthe viewer you mean when several are open. `capture_targets` supplies the exact\ncapture arguments for each visible matching viewer; use the chosen target\nwithout adding a guessed view epoch. Pass the inspected revision to\nupdates, then capture the new revision with `capture_a2ui_surface`. Its result\nattaches real pixels to your next model step and retains a hashed image artifact\nwith the viewer state. For a saved dashboard, pass its immutable `artifact_id`\nto inspection and capture. Review a temporary live surface when you need to\nchange a saved definition; publish the reviewed document as a new version.\nTo navigate or change declared controls in an open saved dashboard, use\n`update_a2ui_data_model` with its `artifact_id`, surface/revision, selected\n`viewer_id` and inspected `expected_view_revision`. This changes only that\nview's local binding. Inspect its acknowledgement and capture the new epoch;\nit does not edit the immutable artifact or submit a question answer.\nBind `Tabs.activeTab` to review each tab; its value is a tab child id.\nBind `clio.map.v1.camera` to pan, zoom or rotate a map, sharing the path when\nviews should move together. Keep reference-backed queries and selections\nauthoritative. An image URI, export link or unrelated earlier screenshot is\nnot visual inspection. Verify the capture's revision and state before reasoning.\nUse the inspected component's exact binding path; map and mesh cameras can\nhave different paths and shapes in the same dashboard. Change that binding\ninstead of replacing the root data model with a guessed set of properties.\nCompare the actual captured camera, frame and filters with the requested\nvalues. If a declared control did not move, inspect its binding and correct\nthe update, then capture again before claiming the change worked.\nIf a viewer is still loading, pass `expected_view_revision=null` (or omit it)\nto let capture wait for readiness within its deadline. Pin a view epoch\nwhen an already-ready human view must match exactly; a loading epoch\nintentionally becomes stale as tiles or layout finish.\nAfter publication, the newly opened viewer can still be mounting. A single\n`a2ui_view_stale` or `a2ui_render_not_ready` result is not the end of the review:\ninspect the same immutable artifact again and retry capture with its current\nviewer. If `ready` is false, pass `expected_view_revision=null` rather than guessing\nzero. Retry at most twice for each requested view; stop and report the actual limitation if the viewer\nis absent or still cannot supply pixels. After each successful declared tab or\ncamera change, use the acknowledged epoch or inspect afresh before capture.\nIf capture or a requested control is unavailable, make supported structural\ncorrections and state the remaining verification limit; do not fabricate a\ncapture or describe a map camera as controllable because the person can zoom it.\n\nInspect at the size the person will use. Check the overview, relevant tabs,\nlabels, legends, units, contrast, clipping, framing and controls. Ask whether\nthe view answers the question and is valuable to a human: can the reader find\nthe important comparison without deciphering a dense wall of marks?\nAlso review the explanation: what conclusion can a person see in this image,\nwhich marks support it, and what uncertainty remains? Compare related panels'\ncategory meanings, ranges, dates and selected records. Use direct labels or\nreference marks where they reduce the effort of finding the evidence. Remove\nredundant panels and give the central comparison more space. Load the dashboard\nskill's `references/report-design.md` when composing a substantial report.\nCheck composition as a whole: can related charts, images, viewports and text\nbe interpreted together without tab switching? Review a whole-report image,\nnot only individual views. Preserve unequal row proportions when expanded\nand readable stacking when docked. Optional tabs must not hide essential\nevidence from the initial view or PNG.\nPerform this review yourself before presenting a complex visual; the person\nshould not need to request a screenshot check separately.\nWhen a view is crowded, show the meaningful subset or aggregate first. Retain\nthe complete source data and explain the initial slice. Make additional series,\nlayers or views available through catalog-supported selectors, filters, tabs\nor optional-view controls, with readable labels and visible inclusion state.\nDo not invent a visibility property or hide contrary evidence to improve the\nstory. Check the revealed detail as well as the quiet default.\n\nUse annotations to point to evidence during explanations and questions.\nUpdate a chart with supported layered marks for a labelled point, red outline,\nrange or trend; keep the original rows and quantitative encodings intact.\nUse real data coordinates or stable entity IDs when a mark should follow\nzoom/filter changes. A pixel-positioned mark belongs to one captured viewport;\ndo not reuse it on a different view as if it still identifies the same data.\nAnnotations clarify evidence; they do not change measurements or submit an\nanswer. `ask_user` continues to own question submission independently.\n\nFor worked decision patterns, load `references/investigation-patterns.md`\nfrom this skill. Stop once the question is resolved and the relevant views\nare readable; further captures should answer a remaining concern. Keep visual\nobservations, calculations and unresolved uncertainty distinct in the answer.\n\nKeep the final response focused on the requested deliverables and findings.\n`capture_a2ui_surface` retains its screenshots as verification evidence; do not\nregister or list each capture as another output. For other review images/PDFs,\nuse `create_artifact(..., purpose=\"verification\")`; working files use\n`purpose=\"intermediate\"`. Both remain accessible in Observability and lineage.\nRequested images/PDFs use `purpose=\"deliverable\"`. When revising an output,\nkeep its artifact family/name; the response presents its latest deliverable\nversion while Versions and Observability retain earlier attempts.\n\nBundled files (use file=... for one or files=[...] for a batch):\n- examples/annotated-scatter.json\n- references/investigation-patterns.md","presentation":{"subject":"skill-name","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"skill-name","type":"text","media_type":"","text":"review-visual-presentation","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"content","type":"markdown","media_type":"","text":"Skill directory (use as SKILL_ROOT): D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\clio-ndp-source\\src\\clio_agent\\gact\\builtin_skills\\review-visual-presentation\nUse visual interaction to investigate a question and to improve what a person\nwill see. The loop is: inspect the evidence and current view, change a declared\ncontrol or component, inspect the resulting image, reason, and refine.\nChoose changes that resolve a concrete uncertainty or presentation problem.\nThis applies to maps, charts, tables, images, models and interconnected reports.\n\nFor a substantial authored dashboard or diagram, close this concrete loop:\n\n1. Open the actual published viewer, inspect its current capture target, and\n   capture the overview at the width the person will use.\n2. Look at the returned image, not just its URI, source JSON or tool success.\n   Check whether the main idea is apparent, text is readable, the whole diagram\n   fits, and empty space or narrow columns obscure relationships. Ask whether\n   a full-width view, equal panels or a simpler arrangement would explain it better.\n   Include the surrounding frame/component headings, not only the plotted marks:\n   a title cut off with an ellipsis is a defect even when the graph fits. Check\n   whether labels can actually be read at this size, rather than merely seen.\n3. Identify a concrete defect and change the source or a declared view control.\n   Changing column counts is useful only when it fixes the observed problem.\n4. Capture the revised view and inspect its image to confirm the correction.\n   Check an expanded view as well when the docked and expanded arrangements differ.\n5. Exercise important declared controls or linked selections. For a workflow\n   folder link, verify the target with filesystem tools. If interaction tools are\n   available, check that clicking selects that folder in Files. Claim a navigation\n   check only when it was observed; a highlighted box alone does not prove it.\n\nRepeat while a material defect remains. State the actual visual checks and any\nunresolved limitation. Schema validation, a capture receipt and an uninspected\nimage do not establish visual quality. A small inline diagram does not require\nbuilding a dashboard or following an elaborate layout recipe.\nKeep docked and expanded findings separate: readability in an expanded image\ndoes not establish readability in a narrow pane. When text remains too small,\nrevise the view or state that limitation instead of declaring the review clear.\n\nRead the current surface with `inspect_a2ui_surface` and load the relevant\nactive catalog schemas. `update_a2ui_components` replaces complete definitions\nfor the named components; preserve the other properties, references and links.\n`update_a2ui_data_model` changes a declared binding. Reuse shared filter and\nselection semantics rather than inventing another interaction model. For definition\nchanges to saved dashboards, edit the source document and publish a new immutable version.\n\nDistinguish server state from a rendered view. A producer's `rendered=true`\nmeans the definition was accepted, not that you inspected its pixels.\n`inspect_a2ui_surface` reports fresh mounted viewers, declared bindings,\ncurrent values, cameras, active tabs, data references and readiness. Choose\nthe viewer you mean when several are open. `capture_targets` supplies the exact\ncapture arguments for each visible matching viewer; use the chosen target\nwithout adding a guessed view epoch. Pass the inspected revision to\nupdates, then capture the new revision with `capture_a2ui_surface`. Its result\nattaches real pixels to your next model step and retains a hashed image artifact\nwith the viewer state. For a saved dashboard, pass its immutable `artifact_id`\nto inspection and capture. Review a temporary live surface when you need to\nchange a saved definition; publish the reviewed document as a new version.\nTo navigate or change declared controls in an open saved dashboard, use\n`update_a2ui_data_model` with its `artifact_id`, surface/revision, selected\n`viewer_id` and inspected `expected_view_revision`. This changes only that\nview's local binding. Inspect its acknowledgement and capture the new epoch;\nit does not edit the immutable artifact or submit a question answer.\nBind `Tabs.activeTab` to review each tab; its value is a tab child id.\nBind `clio.map.v1.camera` to pan, zoom or rotate a map, sharing the path when\nviews should move together. Keep reference-backed queries and selections\nauthoritative. An image URI, export link or unrelated earlier screenshot is\nnot visual inspection. Verify the capture's revision and state before reasoning.\nUse the inspected component's exact binding path; map and mesh cameras can\nhave different paths and shapes in the same dashboard. Change that binding\ninstead of replacing the root data model with a guessed set of properties.\nCompare the actual captured camera, frame and filters with the requested\nvalues. If a declared control did not move, inspect its binding and correct\nthe update, then capture again before claiming the change worked.\nIf a viewer is still loading, pass `expected_view_revision=null` (or omit it)\nto let capture wait for readiness within its deadline. Pin a view epoch\nwhen an already-ready human view must match exactly; a loading epoch\nintentionally becomes stale as tiles or layout finish.\nAfter publication, the newly opened viewer can still be mounting. A single\n`a2ui_view_stale` or `a2ui_render_not_ready` result is not the end of the review:\ninspect the same immutable artifact again and retry capture with its current\nviewer. If `ready` is false, pass `expected_view_revision=null` rather than guessing\nzero. Retry at most twice for each requested view; stop and report the actual limitation if the viewer\nis absent or still cannot supply pixels. After each successful declared tab or\ncamera change, use the acknowledged epoch or inspect afresh before capture.\nIf capture or a requested control is unavailable, make supported structural\ncorrections and state the remaining verification limit; do not fabricate a\ncapture or describe a map camera as controllable because the person can zoom it.\n\nInspect at the size the person will use. Check the overview, relevant tabs,\nlabels, legends, units, contrast, clipping, framing and controls. Ask whether\nthe view answers the question and is valuable to a human: can the reader find\nthe important comparison without deciphering a dense wall of marks?\nAlso review the explanation: what conclusion can a person see in this image,\nwhich marks support it, and what uncertainty remains? Compare related panels'\ncategory meanings, ranges, dates and selected records. Use direct labels or\nreference marks where they reduce the effort of finding the evidence. Remove\nredundant panels and give the central comparison more space. Load the dashboard\nskill's `references/report-design.md` when composing a substantial report.\nCheck composition as a whole: can related charts, images, viewports and text\nbe interpreted together without tab switching? Review a whole-report image,\nnot only individual views. Preserve unequal row proportions when expanded\nand readable stacking when docked. Optional tabs must not hide essential\nevidence from the initial view or PNG.\nPerform this review yourself before presenting a complex visual; the person\nshould not need to request a screenshot check separately.\nWhen a view is crowded, show the meaningful subset or aggregate first. Retain\nthe complete source data and explain the initial slice. Make additional series,\nlayers or views available through catalog-supported selectors, filters, tabs\nor optional-view controls, with readable labels and visible inclusion state.\nDo not invent a visibility property or hide contrary evidence to improve the\nstory. Check the revealed detail as well as the quiet default.\n\nUse annotations to point to evidence during explanations and questions.\nUpdate a chart with supported layered marks for a labelled point, red outline,\nrange or trend; keep the original rows and quantitative encodings intact.\nUse real data coordinates or stable entity IDs when a mark should follow\nzoom/filter changes. A pixel-positioned mark belongs to one captured viewport;\ndo not reuse it on a different view as if it still identifies the same data.\nAnnotations clarify evidence; they do not change measurements or submit an\nanswer. `ask_user` continues to own question submission independently.\n\nFor worked decision patterns, load `references/investigation-patterns.md`\nfrom this skill. Stop once the question is resolved and the relevant views\nare readable; further captures should answer a remaining concern. Keep visual\nobservations, calculations and unresolved uncertainty distinct in the answer.\n\nKeep the final response focused on the requested deliverables and findings.\n`capture_a2ui_surface` retains its screenshots as verification evidence; do not\nregister or list each capture as another output. For other review images/PDFs,\nuse `create_artifact(..., purpose=\"verification\")`; working files use\n`purpose=\"intermediate\"`. Both remain accessible in Observability and lineage.\nRequested images/PDFs use `purpose=\"deliverable\"`. When revising an output,\nkeep its artifact family/name; the response presents its latest deliverable\nversion while Versions and Observability retain earlier attempts.\n\nBundled files (use file=... for one or files=[...] for a batch):\n- examples/annotated-scatter.json\n- references/investigation-patterns.md","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":369.0822124481201,"started_at":"2026-10-19T07:10:30.150323+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:10:30.519405+00:00"},{"id":"call_0bb5841c7804","session_id":"sess_4e74d38f7a9d","run_id":"76bc3ce2-4dce-44cb-93e0-3b57b07a3203","name":"load_skill","title":"Load skill","state":"succeeded","input":{"kwargs":{"file":"","files":["catalog.json#/components/clio.chart.v1","catalog.json#/components/clio.data-table.v1","catalog.json#/components/ChoicePicker","catalog.json#/components/Column","catalog.json#/components/Text","catalog.json#/components/clio.slider.v1"],"skill_id":"a2ui-catalog-clio-workspace"}},"output":"=== File 1/6: catalog.json#/components/clio.chart.v1 ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"dependentRequired\": {\n        \"dataQuery\": [\n          \"dataUri\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"colorField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"clio.chart.v1\"\n        },\n        \"data\": {\n          \"description\": \"Inline rows (at most 10000) \\u2014 this array rides the surface's own wire message, so it is capped for transfer size; for a larger or growing dataset use dataUri instead, unbounded and paged/downsampled by the viewer. A cell is a scalar OR a strictly-shaped GeoJSON Geometry object ($defs/GeoJsonGeometry), so a geoshape mark can draw real shapes from inline rows.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"additionalProperties\": {\n              \"anyOf\": [\n                {\n                  \"type\": [\n                    \"string\",\n                    \"number\",\n                    \"boolean\",\n                    \"null\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                {\n                  \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/GeoJsonGeometry\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 10000,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"dataQuery\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DataQuery\"\n        },\n        \"dataUri\": {\n          \"description\": \"A workspace file path or artifact:// reference; CLIO registers a path as an artifact before validation.\",\n          \"not\": {\n            \"pattern\": \"\\\\s\"\n          },\n          \"pattern\": \"^artifact://artifact_[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"entityField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"facetField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"height\": {\n          \"maximum\": 2000,\n          \"minimum\": 80,\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"preset\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"trajectories\",\n            \"heatmap\",\n            \"spectra\",\n            \"boxplot\",\n            \"scatter\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"selection\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\",\n          \"description\": \"Bind to /selection/<key>; the bound value is a SelectionState ({field, values[], source?}, see $defs/SelectionState). Components bound to the same path share one selection.\"\n        },\n        \"selectionField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\",\n          \"description\": \"Column used for an explicit selection binding. Ordinary views of one dataUri link by __row without this property; trajectory and spectra points select exact rows while entityField groups each curve.\"\n        },\n        \"selectionParam\": {\n          \"default\": \"sel\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"spec\": {\n          \"allOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecDataNamedSource\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"description\": \"A Vega-Lite spec whose rows come from data/dataUri as the named dataset 'source' \\u2014 the spec is chart configuration, never a data channel, and the dataset itself is unbounded via dataUri regardless of this cap. This schema already enforces the top-level key allowlist, no url/usermeta key at any depth, no bind.element at any depth (a CSS selector that could mount an input widget anywhere on the host page), and data only as {name: source} at any depth; the renderer additionally enforces the config-size (65536 bytes) and view-count (8) caps that keep the spec itself bounded and abuse-resistant, which JSON Schema cannot express. See a2ui/chart/guard_rules.json.\",\n          \"propertyNames\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"$schema\",\n              \"mark\",\n              \"encoding\",\n              \"layer\",\n              \"facet\",\n              \"hconcat\",\n              \"vconcat\",\n              \"concat\",\n              \"repeat\",\n              \"spec\",\n              \"transform\",\n              \"params\",\n              \"width\",\n              \"height\",\n              \"title\",\n              \"resolve\",\n              \"config\",\n              \"autosize\",\n              \"description\",\n              \"columns\",\n              \"spacing\",\n              \"padding\",\n              \"align\",\n              \"bounds\",\n              \"center\",\n              \"projection\",\n              \"data\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"title\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"xField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"xType\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"temporal\",\n            \"quantitative\",\n            \"ordinal\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"yField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Exactly one of spec or preset; preset fill fields need preset.\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"preset\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"xField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"yField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"entityField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"colorField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"facetField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"xType\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"spec\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"spec\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"preset\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Exactly one of data or dataUri is required.\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"dataUri\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"data\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"data\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"dataUri\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the trajectories preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"trajectories\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the heatmap preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"heatmap\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"colorField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the spectra preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"spectra\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the boxplot preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"boxplot\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"required\": [\n                \"facetField\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"required\": [\n                \"xType\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the scatter preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"scatter\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Any chart over tabular rows: a preset or an Altair/Vega-Lite spec.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\n\n=== File 2/6: catalog.json#/components/clio.data-table.v1 ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"dependentRequired\": {\n        \"dataQuery\": [\n          \"dataUri\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"action\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Action\"\n        },\n        \"columns\": {\n          \"description\": \"Required with inline rows; optional with dataUri (defaults to the queried/dataset columns).\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"oneOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DataTableColumn\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"clio.data-table.v1\"\n        },\n        \"dataQuery\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DataQuery\"\n        },\n        \"dataUri\": {\n          \"description\": \"A workspace file path or artifact:// reference; CLIO registers a path as an artifact before validation.\",\n          \"not\": {\n            \"pattern\": \"\\\\s\"\n          },\n          \"pattern\": \"^artifact://artifact_[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"rows\": {\n          \"description\": \"Inline rows; use dataUri instead for a registered dataset.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"selection\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\",\n          \"description\": \"Bind to /selection/<key>; the bound value is a SelectionState ({field, values[], source?}, see $defs/SelectionState). Components bound to the same path share one selection.\"\n        },\n        \"selectionField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\",\n          \"description\": \"Dataset column the shared selection's values are drawn from; required when selection is bound.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Exactly one of rows or dataUri is required.\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"dataUri\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"rows\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"rows\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"dataUri\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"columns is required alongside inline rows.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"rows\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"columns\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"selectionField is required when selection is bound (an object, not a literal).\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"selection\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"selection\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"selectionField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Tabular rows, inline or from a referenced dataset.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Action, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\n\n=== File 3/6: catalog.json#/components/ChoicePicker ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Checkable\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"ChoicePicker\"\n        },\n        \"displayStyle\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"checkbox\",\n            \"chips\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"filterable\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"label\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"options\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ChoiceOption\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicStringList\"\n        },\n        \"variant\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"multipleSelection\",\n            \"mutuallyExclusive\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"options\",\n        \"value\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A single- or multiple-selection picker; bind value to the path an action reads.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Checkable, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicStringList\n\n=== File 4/6: catalog.json#/components/Column ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"align\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"start\",\n            \"center\",\n            \"end\",\n            \"stretch\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"children\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ChildList\"\n        },\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"Column\"\n        },\n        \"justify\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"start\",\n            \"center\",\n            \"end\",\n            \"spaceBetween\",\n            \"spaceAround\",\n            \"spaceEvenly\",\n            \"stretch\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"children\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A vertical layout container for child components.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ChildList, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\n\n=== File 5/6: catalog.json#/components/Text ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"Text\"\n        },\n        \"text\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"variant\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"h1\",\n            \"h2\",\n            \"h3\",\n            \"h4\",\n            \"h5\",\n            \"caption\",\n            \"body\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"text\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A run of text, plain or headed (h1-h5, caption, body).\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\n\n=== File 6/6: catalog.json#/components/clio.slider.v1 ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"clio.slider.v1\"\n        },\n        \"label\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"max\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"min\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"range\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"step\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"unit\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n          \"oneOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicNumber\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"number\"\n              },\n              \"maxItems\": 2,\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"label\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"min\",\n        \"max\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A fractional-step numeric control, or a two-value range, with typed value boxes.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicNumber, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\n\n### Shared by catalog.json\n## Shared definitions (each referenced by name below, defined once for this call)\n\n### $defs/CatalogComponentCommon\n{\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"weight\": {\n      \"description\": \"Relative flex weight of this component inside a Row or Column. Only meaningful as a direct child of one.\",\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/ChoiceOption\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"label\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n    },\n    \"value\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"label\",\n    \"value\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/DataQuery\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"A server-side table query applied to dataUri: the table-query request body (POST /v1/artifacts/{id}/table-query) without format. The server runs filter, then aggregate, then downsample, then sort, then offset/limit. Omit columns to request every column of dataUri \\u2014 except alongside aggregate, where columns is required, since aggregate's output columns (e.g. price_mean) don't exist in the source and so cannot be inferred. limit bounds the rows in ONE response (a transfer size), not the underlying data; offset pages through a larger result across several requests. When a chart or map query would otherwise exceed limit without an explicit downsample, the server instead samples evenly across the full range and reports that it did, rather than silently truncating to the first rows. limit's own maximum here is a generous safety ceiling, not the deployment's real per-response cap, which is server-configured. A viewer (e.g. an interactive data-table) may layer its own user-driven paging/filtering/sorting on top of this dataQuery without replacing it \\u2014 the agent's own filter/aggregate/downsample intent still applies underneath. Shared verbatim by clio.chart.v1, clio.map.v1, and clio.data-table.v1.\",\n  \"if\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"aggregate\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"aggregate\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"aggregate\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QueryAggregate\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"columns\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 64,\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"uniqueItems\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"downsample\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QueryDownsample\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"filter\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QueryFilter\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 64,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limit\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"maximum\": 50000,\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"offset\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"minimum\": 0,\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"sort\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuerySort\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 64,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"required\": [\n      \"columns\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/DataTableColumn\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"key\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"label\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"key\",\n    \"label\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/FieldName\n{\n  \"maxLength\": 128,\n  \"minLength\": 1,\n  \"type\": \"string\"\n}\n\n### $defs/GeoJsonGeometry\n{\n  \"description\": \"A GeoJSON Geometry object (RFC 7946 \\u00a73.1), strictly shaped: Point/MultiPoint/LineString/MultiLineString/Polygon/MultiPolygon carry coordinates; GeometryCollection carries geometries. Never a Feature/FeatureCollection, never a bare coordinate array.\",\n  \"oneOf\": [\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 3,\n          \"minItems\": 2,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"Point\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"number\"\n            },\n            \"maxItems\": 3,\n            \"minItems\": 2,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"MultiPoint\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"number\"\n            },\n            \"maxItems\": 3,\n            \"minItems\": 2,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 2,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"LineString\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"number\"\n              },\n              \"maxItems\": 3,\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"minItems\": 2,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"MultiLineString\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"number\"\n              },\n              \"maxItems\": 3,\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"minItems\": 4,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"Polygon\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": \"number\"\n                },\n                \"maxItems\": 3,\n                \"minItems\": 2,\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              \"minItems\": 4,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"MultiPolygon\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"geometries\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/GeoJsonGeometry\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"GeometryCollection\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"geometries\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QueryAggregate\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"Group rows by groupBy (empty or omitted: one global group) and reduce; each metric becomes a result column named {column}_{fn}, which must not repeat a groupBy column.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"groupBy\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n      },\n      \"maxItems\": 64,\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    },\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"column\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n          },\n          \"fn\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"mean\",\n              \"min\",\n              \"max\",\n              \"count\",\n              \"sum\",\n              \"median\"\n            ],\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"column\",\n          \"fn\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"maxItems\": 64,\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"metrics\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QueryDownsample\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"How the server thins rows before limit applies. none keeps every row; stride keeps evenly spaced rows (per entityColumn up to maxPerEntity when set, else overall up to limit); per_entity_lttb runs LTTB on (x, y) per entityColumn (the whole table is one series without it) and needs x and y.\",\n  \"if\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"mode\": {\n        \"const\": \"per_entity_lttb\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"mode\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"entityColumn\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"maxPerEntity\": {\n      \"default\": 500,\n      \"maximum\": 2000,\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"mode\": {\n      \"default\": \"none\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"none\",\n        \"stride\",\n        \"per_entity_lttb\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"x\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"y\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"x\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"y\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"x\",\n      \"y\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QueryFilter\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"eq\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": [\n                  \"string\",\n                  \"number\",\n                  \"boolean\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"in\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": [\n                    \"string\",\n                    \"number\",\n                    \"boolean\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"maxItems\": 10000,\n                \"minItems\": 1,\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"range\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": [\n                    \"string\",\n                    \"number\",\n                    \"boolean\",\n                    \"null\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"maxItems\": 2,\n                \"minItems\": 2,\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"isnull\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": [\n                  \"boolean\",\n                  \"null\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"contains\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"minLength\": 1,\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"One predicate; all filter entries are AND-ed. eq: value is a non-null scalar. in: value is a non-empty list of scalars. range: value is [min, max], inclusive, either side may be null. isnull: value omitted or true matches nulls, false matches non-nulls. contains: value is a non-empty string, matched as a case-insensitive substring of a string column (a per-column text filter).\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"column\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n    },\n    \"op\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"eq\",\n        \"in\",\n        \"range\",\n        \"isnull\",\n        \"contains\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"value\": {}\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"column\",\n    \"op\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QuerySort\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"One dataQuery.sort key; earlier entries in the list sort first.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"column\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n    },\n    \"desc\": {\n      \"default\": false,\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"column\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/SpecDataNamedSource\n{\n  \"description\": \"Every `data` key anywhere in a Vega-Lite spec is absent or exactly {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source\\\"} \\u2014 rows come from the component's data/dataUri, never the spec.\",\n  \"else\": {\n    \"if\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"then\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecDataNamedSource\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"if\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"additionalProperties\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecDataNamedSource\"\n    },\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"data\": {\n        \"const\": {\n          \"name\": \"source\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n### $defs/SpecNoBindElement\n{\n  \"description\": \"No `element` key inside any `bind` object (params[].bind.element) anywhere in a Vega-Lite spec, at any depth \\u2014 it is a CSS selector that could mount a Vega input widget into any element on the host page, not just this chart.\",\n  \"else\": {\n    \"if\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"then\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"if\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"additionalProperties\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n    },\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"bind\": {\n        \"allOf\": [\n          {\n            \"if\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\"\n            },\n            \"then\": {\n              \"not\": {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"element\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n### $defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\n{\n  \"description\": \"No `url` or `usermeta` key anywhere in a Vega-Lite spec, at any depth.\",\n  \"else\": {\n    \"if\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"then\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"if\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"additionalProperties\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\"\n    },\n    \"not\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"required\": [\n            \"url\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"required\": [\n            \"usermeta\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}","presentation":{"subject":"skill-name","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"skill-name","type":"text","media_type":"","text":"a2ui-catalog-clio-workspace","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"content","type":"markdown","media_type":"","text":"=== File 1/6: catalog.json#/components/clio.chart.v1 ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"dependentRequired\": {\n        \"dataQuery\": [\n          \"dataUri\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"colorField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"clio.chart.v1\"\n        },\n        \"data\": {\n          \"description\": \"Inline rows (at most 10000) \\u2014 this array rides the surface's own wire message, so it is capped for transfer size; for a larger or growing dataset use dataUri instead, unbounded and paged/downsampled by the viewer. A cell is a scalar OR a strictly-shaped GeoJSON Geometry object ($defs/GeoJsonGeometry), so a geoshape mark can draw real shapes from inline rows.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"additionalProperties\": {\n              \"anyOf\": [\n                {\n                  \"type\": [\n                    \"string\",\n                    \"number\",\n                    \"boolean\",\n                    \"null\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                {\n                  \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/GeoJsonGeometry\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 10000,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"dataQuery\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DataQuery\"\n        },\n        \"dataUri\": {\n          \"description\": \"A workspace file path or artifact:// reference; CLIO registers a path as an artifact before validation.\",\n          \"not\": {\n            \"pattern\": \"\\\\s\"\n          },\n          \"pattern\": \"^artifact://artifact_[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"entityField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"facetField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"height\": {\n          \"maximum\": 2000,\n          \"minimum\": 80,\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"preset\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"trajectories\",\n            \"heatmap\",\n            \"spectra\",\n            \"boxplot\",\n            \"scatter\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"selection\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\",\n          \"description\": \"Bind to /selection/<key>; the bound value is a SelectionState ({field, values[], source?}, see $defs/SelectionState). Components bound to the same path share one selection.\"\n        },\n        \"selectionField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\",\n          \"description\": \"Column used for an explicit selection binding. Ordinary views of one dataUri link by __row without this property; trajectory and spectra points select exact rows while entityField groups each curve.\"\n        },\n        \"selectionParam\": {\n          \"default\": \"sel\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"spec\": {\n          \"allOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecDataNamedSource\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"description\": \"A Vega-Lite spec whose rows come from data/dataUri as the named dataset 'source' \\u2014 the spec is chart configuration, never a data channel, and the dataset itself is unbounded via dataUri regardless of this cap. This schema already enforces the top-level key allowlist, no url/usermeta key at any depth, no bind.element at any depth (a CSS selector that could mount an input widget anywhere on the host page), and data only as {name: source} at any depth; the renderer additionally enforces the config-size (65536 bytes) and view-count (8) caps that keep the spec itself bounded and abuse-resistant, which JSON Schema cannot express. See a2ui/chart/guard_rules.json.\",\n          \"propertyNames\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"$schema\",\n              \"mark\",\n              \"encoding\",\n              \"layer\",\n              \"facet\",\n              \"hconcat\",\n              \"vconcat\",\n              \"concat\",\n              \"repeat\",\n              \"spec\",\n              \"transform\",\n              \"params\",\n              \"width\",\n              \"height\",\n              \"title\",\n              \"resolve\",\n              \"config\",\n              \"autosize\",\n              \"description\",\n              \"columns\",\n              \"spacing\",\n              \"padding\",\n              \"align\",\n              \"bounds\",\n              \"center\",\n              \"projection\",\n              \"data\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"title\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"xField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        \"xType\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"temporal\",\n            \"quantitative\",\n            \"ordinal\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"yField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Exactly one of spec or preset; preset fill fields need preset.\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"preset\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"xField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"yField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"entityField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"colorField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"facetField\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"xType\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"spec\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"spec\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"preset\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Exactly one of data or dataUri is required.\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"dataUri\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"data\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"data\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"dataUri\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the trajectories preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"trajectories\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the heatmap preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"heatmap\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"colorField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the spectra preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"spectra\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the boxplot preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"boxplot\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"required\": [\n                \"facetField\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"required\": [\n                \"xType\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fields used by the scatter preset.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"preset\": {\n            \"const\": \"scatter\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"preset\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"xField\",\n          \"yField\",\n          \"entityField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Any chart over tabular rows: a preset or an Altair/Vega-Lite spec.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\n\n=== File 2/6: catalog.json#/components/clio.data-table.v1 ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"dependentRequired\": {\n        \"dataQuery\": [\n          \"dataUri\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"action\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Action\"\n        },\n        \"columns\": {\n          \"description\": \"Required with inline rows; optional with dataUri (defaults to the queried/dataset columns).\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"oneOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DataTableColumn\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"clio.data-table.v1\"\n        },\n        \"dataQuery\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DataQuery\"\n        },\n        \"dataUri\": {\n          \"description\": \"A workspace file path or artifact:// reference; CLIO registers a path as an artifact before validation.\",\n          \"not\": {\n            \"pattern\": \"\\\\s\"\n          },\n          \"pattern\": \"^artifact://artifact_[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"rows\": {\n          \"description\": \"Inline rows; use dataUri instead for a registered dataset.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"selection\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\",\n          \"description\": \"Bind to /selection/<key>; the bound value is a SelectionState ({field, values[], source?}, see $defs/SelectionState). Components bound to the same path share one selection.\"\n        },\n        \"selectionField\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\",\n          \"description\": \"Dataset column the shared selection's values are drawn from; required when selection is bound.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Exactly one of rows or dataUri is required.\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"dataUri\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"rows\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"not\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"rows\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"dataUri\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"columns is required alongside inline rows.\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"rows\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"columns\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"selectionField is required when selection is bound (an object, not a literal).\",\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"selection\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"selection\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"selectionField\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Tabular rows, inline or from a referenced dataset.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Action, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicValue\n\n=== File 3/6: catalog.json#/components/ChoicePicker ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Checkable\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"ChoicePicker\"\n        },\n        \"displayStyle\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"checkbox\",\n            \"chips\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"filterable\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"label\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"options\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ChoiceOption\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicStringList\"\n        },\n        \"variant\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"multipleSelection\",\n            \"mutuallyExclusive\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"options\",\n        \"value\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A single- or multiple-selection picker; bind value to the path an action reads.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/Checkable, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicStringList\n\n=== File 4/6: catalog.json#/components/Column ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"align\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"start\",\n            \"center\",\n            \"end\",\n            \"stretch\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"children\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ChildList\"\n        },\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"Column\"\n        },\n        \"justify\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"start\",\n            \"center\",\n            \"end\",\n            \"spaceBetween\",\n            \"spaceAround\",\n            \"spaceEvenly\",\n            \"stretch\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"children\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A vertical layout container for child components.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ChildList, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\n\n=== File 5/6: catalog.json#/components/Text ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"Text\"\n        },\n        \"text\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"variant\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"h1\",\n            \"h2\",\n            \"h3\",\n            \"h4\",\n            \"h5\",\n            \"caption\",\n            \"body\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"text\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A run of text, plain or headed (h1-h5, caption, body).\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\n\n=== File 6/6: catalog.json#/components/clio.slider.v1 ===\n{\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CatalogComponentCommon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"component\": {\n          \"const\": \"clio.slider.v1\"\n        },\n        \"label\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n        },\n        \"max\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"min\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"range\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"step\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"unit\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n          \"oneOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicNumber\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"number\"\n              },\n              \"maxItems\": 2,\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"component\",\n        \"label\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"min\",\n        \"max\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"A fractional-step numeric control, or a two-value range, with typed value boxes.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"unevaluatedProperties\": false\n}\n\nStandard refs (not loadable here): https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/ComponentCommon, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicNumber, https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\n\n### Shared by catalog.json\n## Shared definitions (each referenced by name below, defined once for this call)\n\n### $defs/CatalogComponentCommon\n{\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"weight\": {\n      \"description\": \"Relative flex weight of this component inside a Row or Column. Only meaningful as a direct child of one.\",\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/ChoiceOption\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"label\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/common_types.json#/$defs/DynamicString\"\n    },\n    \"value\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"label\",\n    \"value\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/DataQuery\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"A server-side table query applied to dataUri: the table-query request body (POST /v1/artifacts/{id}/table-query) without format. The server runs filter, then aggregate, then downsample, then sort, then offset/limit. Omit columns to request every column of dataUri \\u2014 except alongside aggregate, where columns is required, since aggregate's output columns (e.g. price_mean) don't exist in the source and so cannot be inferred. limit bounds the rows in ONE response (a transfer size), not the underlying data; offset pages through a larger result across several requests. When a chart or map query would otherwise exceed limit without an explicit downsample, the server instead samples evenly across the full range and reports that it did, rather than silently truncating to the first rows. limit's own maximum here is a generous safety ceiling, not the deployment's real per-response cap, which is server-configured. A viewer (e.g. an interactive data-table) may layer its own user-driven paging/filtering/sorting on top of this dataQuery without replacing it \\u2014 the agent's own filter/aggregate/downsample intent still applies underneath. Shared verbatim by clio.chart.v1, clio.map.v1, and clio.data-table.v1.\",\n  \"if\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"aggregate\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"aggregate\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"aggregate\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QueryAggregate\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"columns\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 64,\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"uniqueItems\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"downsample\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QueryDownsample\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"filter\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QueryFilter\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 64,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limit\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"maximum\": 50000,\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"offset\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"minimum\": 0,\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"sort\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuerySort\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 64,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"required\": [\n      \"columns\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/DataTableColumn\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"key\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"label\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"key\",\n    \"label\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/FieldName\n{\n  \"maxLength\": 128,\n  \"minLength\": 1,\n  \"type\": \"string\"\n}\n\n### $defs/GeoJsonGeometry\n{\n  \"description\": \"A GeoJSON Geometry object (RFC 7946 \\u00a73.1), strictly shaped: Point/MultiPoint/LineString/MultiLineString/Polygon/MultiPolygon carry coordinates; GeometryCollection carries geometries. Never a Feature/FeatureCollection, never a bare coordinate array.\",\n  \"oneOf\": [\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"maxItems\": 3,\n          \"minItems\": 2,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"Point\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"number\"\n            },\n            \"maxItems\": 3,\n            \"minItems\": 2,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"MultiPoint\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"number\"\n            },\n            \"maxItems\": 3,\n            \"minItems\": 2,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 2,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"LineString\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"number\"\n              },\n              \"maxItems\": 3,\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"minItems\": 2,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"MultiLineString\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"number\"\n              },\n              \"maxItems\": 3,\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"minItems\": 4,\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"Polygon\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"coordinates\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"items\": {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": \"number\"\n                },\n                \"maxItems\": 3,\n                \"minItems\": 2,\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              \"minItems\": 4,\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"MultiPolygon\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"coordinates\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"geometries\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/GeoJsonGeometry\"\n          },\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"GeometryCollection\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"geometries\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QueryAggregate\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"Group rows by groupBy (empty or omitted: one global group) and reduce; each metric becomes a result column named {column}_{fn}, which must not repeat a groupBy column.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"groupBy\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n      },\n      \"maxItems\": 64,\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    },\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"column\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n          },\n          \"fn\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"mean\",\n              \"min\",\n              \"max\",\n              \"count\",\n              \"sum\",\n              \"median\"\n            ],\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"column\",\n          \"fn\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"maxItems\": 64,\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"metrics\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QueryDownsample\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"How the server thins rows before limit applies. none keeps every row; stride keeps evenly spaced rows (per entityColumn up to maxPerEntity when set, else overall up to limit); per_entity_lttb runs LTTB on (x, y) per entityColumn (the whole table is one series without it) and needs x and y.\",\n  \"if\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"mode\": {\n        \"const\": \"per_entity_lttb\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"mode\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"entityColumn\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"maxPerEntity\": {\n      \"default\": 500,\n      \"maximum\": 2000,\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"mode\": {\n      \"default\": \"none\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"none\",\n        \"stride\",\n        \"per_entity_lttb\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"x\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"y\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"x\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"y\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"x\",\n      \"y\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QueryFilter\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"eq\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": [\n                  \"string\",\n                  \"number\",\n                  \"boolean\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"in\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": [\n                    \"string\",\n                    \"number\",\n                    \"boolean\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"maxItems\": 10000,\n                \"minItems\": 1,\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"range\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": [\n                    \"string\",\n                    \"number\",\n                    \"boolean\",\n                    \"null\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"maxItems\": 2,\n                \"minItems\": 2,\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"isnull\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": [\n                  \"boolean\",\n                  \"null\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"contains\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"value\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"minLength\": 1,\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"path\": {\n                    \"pattern\": \"^/\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"path\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"value\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"One predicate; all filter entries are AND-ed. eq: value is a non-null scalar. in: value is a non-empty list of scalars. range: value is [min, max], inclusive, either side may be null. isnull: value omitted or true matches nulls, false matches non-nulls. contains: value is a non-empty string, matched as a case-insensitive substring of a string column (a per-column text filter).\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"column\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n    },\n    \"op\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"eq\",\n        \"in\",\n        \"range\",\n        \"isnull\",\n        \"contains\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"value\": {}\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"column\",\n    \"op\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/QuerySort\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"One dataQuery.sort key; earlier entries in the list sort first.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"column\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FieldName\"\n    },\n    \"desc\": {\n      \"default\": false,\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"column\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n\n### $defs/SpecDataNamedSource\n{\n  \"description\": \"Every `data` key anywhere in a Vega-Lite spec is absent or exactly {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source\\\"} \\u2014 rows come from the component's data/dataUri, never the spec.\",\n  \"else\": {\n    \"if\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"then\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecDataNamedSource\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"if\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"additionalProperties\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecDataNamedSource\"\n    },\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"data\": {\n        \"const\": {\n          \"name\": \"source\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n### $defs/SpecNoBindElement\n{\n  \"description\": \"No `element` key inside any `bind` object (params[].bind.element) anywhere in a Vega-Lite spec, at any depth \\u2014 it is a CSS selector that could mount a Vega input widget into any element on the host page, not just this chart.\",\n  \"else\": {\n    \"if\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"then\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"if\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"additionalProperties\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n    },\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"bind\": {\n        \"allOf\": [\n          {\n            \"if\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\"\n            },\n            \"then\": {\n              \"not\": {\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"element\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoBindElement\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n### $defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\n{\n  \"description\": \"No `url` or `usermeta` key anywhere in a Vega-Lite spec, at any depth.\",\n  \"else\": {\n    \"if\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"then\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SpecNoForbiddenKeys\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"if\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"then\": {\n    \"ad